Abstract = {The paper focuses on determination of the wind threshold velocity of
   re-suspension (at the height of 10 m) and the near-ground air threshold
   velocity of re-suspension (at the height of 0.25 m) for particles of
   size 10 mu m in a particular urban street canyon with two-way traffic.
   The wind threshold velocity of re-suspension is derived from a long-term
   measurement carried out in the city of Brno. A numerical modelling based
   on the finite volume method is used for a detail study of the relation
   between a wind velocity above buildings roofs and a near-ground air
   velocity in the street canyon.},
