Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {The opportunity, challenge and countermeasures faced by city group
   passenger transportation of railway (or rail traffic) are studied. The
   impacts of trip distance with urbanization and city agglomeration
   development are analyzed. Due to the obvious technical and economic
   advantages compared to other transport modes, railway (or rail traffic)
   should play an more important role in city agglomeration passenger
   transportation system pursuing resource saving and friendly environment.
   On the basis of the successful practices and experiences abroad, the
   challenge faced by railway (or rail traffic) and policies that should be
   taken in city group passenger transportation system in China are
   analyzed. At last an empirical study on the Changsha-Zhuzhou-Xiangtan
   city group is conducted.},
