Note = {2024 International Conference on Geographic Perspectives on Climate
   Change Mitigation in Urban and Rural Environments-GCUE, Lecce, ITALY,
   JUN 25-27, 2024},
Organization = {University of Salento},
Abstract = {Education is a unique opportunity to confront the climate crisis, and it
   is necessary to ask how we can prepare undergraduate tourism students
   for mitigating and adapting to climate change. This study's aim was to
   determine how the education of undergraduate tourism students can play a
   key role in mitigating climate change through tourism entrepreneurship
   at the local level. The research had a qualitative and applied design,
   using theoretical and empirical didactic methods. The methodology was
   supported by developing a learning experience in the subject of tourism
   and the environment with 66 students enrolled in the Bachelor's degree
   in tourism at the Autonomous University of Ciudad Juarez in Mexico
   between 2021 and 2023. Eighteen nature hotels were proposed by students,
   incorporating bio-architecture solutions and environmental technologies
   to promote sustainable tourism development and contribute to minimizing
   the adverse impacts of climate change. In this activity, the
   project-based learning approach was implemented. Through their work, the
   students demonstrated that education is a key factor in climate change
   mitigation by making innovative proposals with viable solutions for
   climate change adaptation. These solutions were presented through
   investigative reports using posters and the manual creation of
   sustainable models for nature hotels that respond to the challenges
   induced by changes in temperature and climate patterns.},
