   Assoc Disaster Prevent, Risk Anal Council},
Abstract = {With the rapid urbanization in the world, the urban ecosystems are under
   multiple great pressures. This paper takes the Shenzhen River-Bay Area
   as the case study, the main risk sources in this area are identified and
   a comprehensive risk assessment indices system is established. Based on
   the Pressure-Effect-Social Response (PESR) theory, the risk indices for
   each sub-ecosystem are calculated. The risk grading and the potential
   ecological hazards for the Shenzhen River-Bay area could be determined
   finally. The results of this study could provide the scientific basis
   for risk prevention management in the rapid urbanized regions.},
